sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant API@{ "type": "control" } as Dictaphone API
    participant Reencoder@{ "type": "control" } as HTTP re-encoding worker
    participant Validator@{ "type": "control" } as HTTP validation worker
    participant DB@{ "type": "database" } as PostgreSQL
    participant Queue@{ "type": "queue" } as Redis and Celery queue
    participant Backend@{ "type": "control" } as Backend worker
    participant FileStore@{ "type": "database" } as File-linked object storage
    participant Summary@{ "type": "boundary" } as Summary service

    Reencoder->>API: GET /audio-jobs/transcoding/next<br/>Bearer token
    API-->>Reencoder: 204 or job id, source_url, destination_url
    Reencoder->>FileStore: GET source_url, transcode with FFmpeg,<br/>PUT destination_url
    Reencoder->>API: POST /audio-jobs/transcoding/complete<br/>id and status<br/>duration_seconds on success or error on failure
    API->>DB: Record transcoding result and duration<br/>make validation job available on success
    Validator->>API: GET /audio-jobs/validation/next<br/>Bearer token
    API-->>Validator: 204 or job id, source_url
    Validator->>FileStore: GET source_url and validate with opusinfo + opusdec
    Validator->>API: POST /audio-jobs/validation/complete<br/>id, status, error on failure
    API->>DB: Mark EXTRACTION_DONE after validation succeeds
    API->>Queue: call_transcribe_service.delay(file_id)<br/>queue: dictaphone-backend
    Queue->>Backend: call_transcribe_service(file_id)<br/>queue: dictaphone-backend
    Backend->>DB: Create PENDING transcription job
    Backend->>FileStore: Generate signed GET URL for derived audio
    Backend->>Summary: POST /api/v2/async-jobs/transcribe

    alt Transcription request failure
        Summary-->>Backend: Request failure
        Backend->>DB: Mark transcription job FAILED
    else Transcription request succeeds
        Summary-->>Backend: 200 pending and remote job id
        Backend->>DB: Save remote transcription job id
    end

    Note over Reencoder,Validator: Worker polling, signed URLs, validation, and completion callbacks are detailed in their dedicated sequence diagrams.
